TITLE: Complete Rust Search Function Implementation
DESCRIPTION: The final implementation of the search function that collects and returns all lines containing the query string. It stores matching lines in a vector and returns it.
SOURCE: https://github.com/rust-lang/book/blob/main/src/ch12-04-testing-the-librarys-functionality.md#2025-04-08_snippet_4

LANGUAGE: rust
CODE:
```
pub fn search<'a>(query: &str, contents: &'a str) -> Vec<&'a str> {
    let mut results = Vec::new();

    for line in contents.lines() {
        if line.contains(query) {
            results.push(line);
        }
    }

    results
}
```

